# Draft-commit git-log style (persistent)

This file was written by `/crav1-draft-commit-message` when you chose **existing git log style, this commit and onward**.

When drafting or creating commits in this repo:

- Match **this repository’s** recent `git log` (subjects and bodies), not `crav1-draft-commit-message/references/style.md`.
- Do not switch to Conventional Commits unless the live log already uses that shape.
- Do not ask whether to use git-log style. It stays on until this rule is removed.

**To stop and get the style prompt again:** delete this file. Cursor: `.cursor/rules/draft-commit-gitlog.mdc`. Claude Code project: `.claude/rules/draft-commit-gitlog.md`. Claude Code user: `~/.claude/rules/draft-commit-gitlog.md`. Nothing else to undo.

Only one draft-commit persist rule should exist. If another one is also present, delete one of them. Cursor style file: `.cursor/rules/draft-commit-style.mdc` (legacy `.cursor/rules/gitkraken-commit-style.mdc`). Claude Code project: `.claude/rules/draft-commit-style.md` (legacy `.claude/rules/gitkraken-commit-style.md`). Claude Code user: `~/.claude/rules/draft-commit-style.md` (legacy `~/.claude/rules/gitkraken-commit-style.md`).
